  "name": "Maya Pax (Quintana Roo Maya ceremonial music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ceremonial music of the Maya of the Cruzo'ob shrine centres of central Quintana Roo, in the municipalities of Felipe Carrillo Puerto and Tulum, played as an offering to the Holy Cross at fiestas and rituals; the term maya pax covers the music, its instruments, the dance and its performers. The ensemble joins the Maya violin with the tarola snare drum, the bombo bass drum and a cane flute. The Quintana Roo state legislature has declared it intangible cultural heritage of the state. The generic drum card stands in for the bombo and the generic flute card for the cane flute.",
